## Michael's Memo: No Brackets, Just Business

March isn't just about buzzer-beaters and Cinderella stories. It's about momentum. In business and basketball, it's the team with the right strategy and trusted teammates who advance. At Serve Funding, that's what we're here for.

This month I want to highlight a client story that reflects our ethos perfectly: a Florida-based medical device company that turned a close call at the bank into a $3.35MM working capital win, all because someone who knew them made an introduction.

Growth isn't always linear, and it rarely fits neatly into a box. That's why we build creative capital solutions that meet our clients where they are and get them where they want to go.

Let's keep moving forward,

Michael

## Client Spotlight: From Coverage Shortfall to $3.35MM in Capital

A five-year-old, growth-stage medical device manufacturer in Central Florida had just missed qualifying for traditional financing on a narrow debt-service-coverage shortfall. They needed capital to support net-60 customer terms, deepen inventory for large orders, and refinance friendly investors.

Over nine months, Serve Funding closed a sequence of facilities for this client: a $400K unsecured term loan, a $1MM receivables revolver at 92% advance and Prime + 2 that later grew to $1.5MM as revenue surged, two refinances of the original loan with cash out, a $550K second mortgage to retire friends-and-family money, and, in January, our first direct capital injection from our own family funds to get inventory out of China ahead of new tariffs.

The result: 30%+ year-over-year revenue growth and $5MM+ in 2024 revenue. The full story, tranche by tranche, is in the case study: [$3.35MM in Game-Changing Capital](/blog/medical-device-growth-story).

{% callout type="tip" title="Skin in the game" %}
At Serve Funding, we don't just advise from the sidelines. When it counts, we commit capital and put our own skin in the game to help our clients grow.
{% /callout %}

## More Than Money: Our Core Values Spell T.R.U.S.T.

At Serve Funding, relationships aren't transactional. They're transformational. The business owners and advisors we work with choose us again and again because of the values we live by:

- **Transparency.** We communicate with clarity and honesty in every interaction. Trust starts with the truth.
- **Responsibility.** We follow through on every commitment, staying accountable to our word.
- **Understanding.** We actively listen to ensure we fully grasp your unique needs and goals.
- **Service.** Our servant-leadership approach prioritizes win-win outcomes and long-term success.
- **Thankfulness.** We operate with deep gratitude for every conversation, introduction, and opportunity to serve.

